# Supabase SQL Source of Truth

When changing the Supabase/Postgres database, always update the greenfield deploy scripts in the same change (same PR/commit as the migration or `af_*.sql` edit).

## Schema (tables, columns, indexes, RLS, seed data)

- **Canonical file:** `sql/supabase_schema_create.sql`
- **Also add:** a one-off migration under `sql/migration_*.sql` when upgrading an existing DB
- **Required:** mirror new columns/constraints in the relevant `CREATE TABLE` (or equivalent) in `supabase_schema_create.sql`, not only in the migration

## Functions (RPCs, triggers implemented as functions)

- **Canonical file:** `sql/supabase_functions_create.sql`
- **Also add:** or update the matching `sql/af_*.sql` (or other function file) for the single-function deploy path
- **Required:** copy the full updated `CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION` (and `DROP`/`GRANT` signature changes) into `supabase_functions_create.sql` so running that script deploys the latest functions

## Checklist before finishing SQL work

1. Migration file exists (if the change is not greenfield-only)
2. `supabase_schema_create.sql` reflects the new schema
3. `supabase_functions_create.sql` reflects any changed function bodies or signatures
4. Old function signatures are dropped where signatures changed (see top-of-file `DROP FUNCTION` block in `supabase_functions_create.sql` when applicable)

Do not treat migrations or individual `af_*.sql` files alone as sufficient for a fresh database or full function redeploy.
